@startuml A3-analysis-interaction-diagram
title UC-ADM-02 – Analysis interaction diagram (boundary / control / entity)
actor "System administrator" as Admin
boundary "Role management view" as View
control "Role administration" as Ctrl
entity User
entity Role
entity Permission
entity AuditEvent

== Main flow ==
Admin -> View : 1. locate user account
View -> Ctrl : find user
Ctrl -> Permission : 0. check requester holds "manage roles and permissions"
Ctrl -> User : read assignments and status
Ctrl --> View : 2. current role assignments, account status
Admin -> View : 3. select or change role assignment
View -> Ctrl : request change
Ctrl -> Role : 4. validate against available roles and rules\n(user must keep at least one role)
Ctrl --> View : validation result
Admin -> View : 5. review and confirm
View -> Ctrl : confirm change
Ctrl -> User : 6. save assignment
Ctrl -> AuditEvent : record change (attributable)
Ctrl --> View : confirmation of effective result

== Alternative flows ==
alt A1 requester lacks the permission (any role not granting it)
  Ctrl --> View : rejected, assignment unchanged
else A2 invalid role or access rule
  Ctrl --> View : explanation, assignment unchanged
else A4 sensitive assignment
  Ctrl --> View : safeguards required before saving
else A3 save failure
  Ctrl --> View : failure reported, access not changed
end
@enduml
